rump  kernel  (librumpvfs,  -lrumpvfs) is a simple in‐memory file
system for rump kernels.  It is automatically mounted as the root
file system of a rump kernel at boot time, provided that the  VFS
faction  is  configured into the rump kernel instance.  The three
main features of are: providing a hook for accessing  host  files
via  the interfaces.  supporting enough of file and directory in‐
terfaces to facilitate simple operations such as  hosting  config
files  or  creating mount points.  being small and lightweight so
as to keep a barebones rump kernel lightweight.  is not  intended
for  hosting  large files or big directory hierarchies.  If faced
with such a use case, mounting a tmpfs  file  system  inside  the
